From 59f12e1dabe0eae5afc525c1826cd110ea183ba8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raiju contributors <raiju@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:29:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Bun.udpSocket for datagrams, and node:dgram over the
 same sockets

Tov had no datagram sockets, so node:dgram was a stub. Bun.udpSocket opens a UDP socket
bound to hostname and port: its socket.data gets each datagram whole, with the sender's
port and address, and send(text | bytes, port, address) returns whether the datagram went.
Options (broadcast, reusePort, TTL, multicast loopback and interface) and multicast
membership are as in Bun.

A socket is an entry in the socket table of runtime/net.c, watched by the same loop as
TCP and Unix sockets. It keeps the program running while it reads, unless it is unref'd.
node:dgram's udp_wrap binding is implemented over the same natives (bind, send, connect,
membership, options, names, recv start and stop, close).

Tests: tests/run/native_udp.tov checks a datagram and its reply with the sender's port
and address, the options, a multicast group joined and left, and that a closed socket
sends nothing.
